{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SubstrateParameter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SubstrateParameter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.GroundRingCore"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantumPlanckConstant_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantumPlanckConstant_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L144-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantumPlanckConstant_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantumPlanckConstant_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L133-L142","doc":"The quantum Planck constant takes values in `[0, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantumPlanckConstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantumPlanckConstant","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L127-L131","doc":"**Quantum Planck constant**: `ℏ_q(p) = 1 − q(p)⁻¹`.\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-planck-constant}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-planck-constant","label":"def:quantum-planck-constant","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-planck-constant.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGaugeGroup.groupAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGaugeGroup.groupAt","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L125-L125","doc":"The quantum group at each point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGaugeGroup.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGaugeGroup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGaugeGroup.toArchimedeanSubstrateField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGaugeGroup.toArchimedeanSubstrateField","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L123-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGaugeGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGaugeGroup","kind":"structure","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L121-L125","doc":"**Quantum gauge group**: the family `{SU_{q(p)}(2)}_{p ∈ M}`.\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-gauge-group}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-gauge-group","label":"def:quantum-gauge-group","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-gauge-group.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_pos","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L105-L119","doc":"**Positivity is derived, not assumed.**\n\nThis was a fourth field, `field_pos`, sitting beside `field_ge_one` — and\n`0 < q` follows from `1 ≤ q` by transitivity with `0 < 1`. Positing both\nmade the structure carry a redundant axiom, which is exactly what the\nco-located sibling avoided: its docstring says the classicality bound is\nthe *single* archimedean axiom, \"from which positivity, invertibility, and\nthe non-negativity of the quantum Planck displacement are derived\".\n\nKept under the same name, so every existing `sp.field_pos p` call site\nreads identically — dot notation resolves to this theorem exactly as it\nresolved to the field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.not_root_of_unity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.not_root_of_unity","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L103-L103","doc":"`q₀(p)` is never a root of unity.\n\nIndependent of `field_ge_one` and so genuinely a field: `q = 1` satisfies\n`1 ≤ q` and *is* a root of unity, so the bound alone does not exclude it.\nNote this is a library-side assumption — `substrate-parameter.md` states\nthe substrate parameter as `q ∈ End(𝟙)` and says nothing about roots of\nunity. Recorded rather than quietly relied on (bean `qou-6ome`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_ge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_ge_one","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L95-L95","doc":"**Classicality bound**: `q(p) ≥ 1` at every point.\n\n`q(p) = 1` is the classical limit (`ℏ_q = 0`); `q(p) > 1` is the quantum\nregime, where the physical substrate sits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L90-L90","doc":"The substrate field `q : M → ℝ` with `q(p) ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.mk","kind":"ctor","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField","kind":"structure","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L67-L103","doc":"**Archimedean substrate field**: the substrate parameter as a genuine real\nfield `q : M → ℝ`.\n\nThis is the structure that used to be called `SubstrateParameter`; the\nrename is about which side of the §7c wall the name advertises, not about\nweakening what is assumed. `field_pos` is the one field that did not\nsurvive as a field — it is derivable, and is a theorem below.\n\n**`field` here is independent by construction.** This docstring used to say\nthe structure was \"obtained by specialising the categorical field through\n`ι : R_q → ℝ, q ↦ q₀`\" — prose asserting a tie the type did not carry.\nNothing related `field` to `SubstrateParameter.field`, so an instance could\npair a real field with an entirely unrelated categorical one.\n\nTo get the specialisation that prose described, build a\n`QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation` and take\n`toArchimedeanSubstrateField`. There `ι` is **constructed**, not assumed\n(`QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean`, bean `qou-d8m1`): `R_q` is\n`LaurentPolynomial ℤ`, so evaluation at a real unit is an ordinary ring\nhom. This bare structure is kept for call sites that need only the\narchimedean data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SubstrateParameter.field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SubstrateParameter.field","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The categorical substrate field `q : M → R_q`. Records the local value\nof the `End(𝟙) ≅ R_q`-element at each point `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SubstrateParameter.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SubstrateParameter.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SubstrateParameter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SubstrateParameter","kind":"structure","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SubstrateParameter.lean#L53-L65","doc":"**Substrate parameter** (categorical), the block's own definition: the\nfibre coordinate `q ∈ End(𝟙)`, recorded pointwise as a field over the\nformal ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`.\n\nUn-ordered by construction. `q(p) > 0`, `q(p) ≥ 1` and \"not a root of\nunity\" are **archimedean** facts and live on `ArchimedeanSubstrateField`\nbelow, past the §7c wall.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:substrate-parameter}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:substrate-parameter","label":"def:substrate-parameter","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}